# Security & privacy (Global)

- Never reveal, hardcode, or log secrets (keys/tokens/passwords/connection strings).
- Use least privilege; avoid admin-wide permissions unless explicitly required.
- Validate/sanitize inputs at boundaries; fail safely with clear errors.
- Don’t roll your own auth/crypto; use framework/repo patterns.
- Avoid logging sensitive data; redact/mask where relevant.
- Be cautious with new public endpoints, file upload/download, webhooks, auth changes:
  - ask targeted questions (within the 2-question budget) if needed to avoid unsafe defaults.
